    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceSteamOfficial">Official Steam: covers and library heroes when the game can be matched to Steam</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceSteamScreenshots">Official Steam screenshots as alternative backgrounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceSteamGridDb">SteamGridDB: community covers, icons and heroes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceSteamGridDbBackgroundGrids">Use horizontal SteamGridDB grids as backgrounds if there are not enough heroes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceRawg">RAWG.io: main image and screenshots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceMobyGames">MobyGames: historical covers and screenshots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceIgdb">IGDB: covers, artworks and screenshots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_MissingApiKeyHelp">If an active source does not have an API key configured, the plugin will automatically skip it when fetching data.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_BackgroundLogoPreference">Logo preference for backgrounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_BackgroundLogoPreferenceHelp">Not all sources expose this information perfectly. The plugin uses it as a preference: if it cannot tell, it chooses the image that best fits the format.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SelectionCriteria">Selection criteria</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AvoidNsfw">Avoid NSFW content when the source marks it</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AvoidBlurred">Avoid blurred styles in covers and backgrounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_PreferOfficial">Prefer official assets when the source indicates it</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AvoidConsoleCovers">Avoid covers with console stripe/logo when possible</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SquareIconPreferGrid">For square icons, prioritize square grids before transparent icons</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SquareIconPreferGridHelp">This last option avoids many round icons or transparent logos: it prioritizes a square image and converts it to a 256x256 icon.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_MaxMediaResults">Maximum results to review per game</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_MaxMediaResultsHelp">How many candidates from all sources are evaluated before choosing the closest one to the preset. Higher values can improve selection, but take a little longer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportNewGames">Import metadata with Metadata AI when new games are detected</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportNewGamesHelp">The plugin remembers existing games and, after a library update, processes only new IDs. It runs after Playnite, so it can overwrite or complete what Playnite downloaded according to the configured apply modes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportGenerateMetadata">Generate text metadata and lists with AI</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportGenerateMetadataHelp">Uses the settings from the AI, Templates, Fields and Rules tabs. If AI is not configured, this part is skipped.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportGenerateMedia">Download media automatically</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportGenerateMediaHelp">Uses the Media tab settings. For Steam games it can use official Steam without a key; SteamGridDB is used as an additional source if an API key is configured.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_AutoImportPlayniteNote">Note: Playnite does not offer a reliable way for a plugin to globally disable its metadata download on import. Metadata AI runs afterwards and follows your overwrite, append or fill-empty rules.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_GenerateAndApply">Generate and apply</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_ExistingOnly">Existing only</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_FieldBehaviorTitle">Field generation and application rules</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_FieldBehaviorHelp">Choose which fields Metadata AI may generate, how each result is applied, and the maximum number of values allowed in list fields.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Maximum">Maximum</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_UseExistingPlayniteValues">Use Playnite values</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_UseExistingPlayniteValuesHelp">• Using Playnite values means that, when enabled, Metadata AI can only select values that already exist in your Playnite database for that field. This prevents nearly identical tags, genres, features, or categories from being created with different wording.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_FieldAccuracyNotesTitle">Accuracy notes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_DeveloperPublisherAccuracyNote">• Developers and publishers: a maximum of 1 keeps only the main credited developer or publisher. Higher limits may include additional credited collaborators when reliable evidence is available.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SortingNameAccuracyNote">• Sorting name: calculated locally from sequel numbering such as 2/3, II/III, or v2/v3 to produce a stable series order such as Base name 01, 02, 03.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_PrefixesTitle">Prefixes for created values</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_BlacklistTitle">Excluded terms</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Description">Description</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Genres">Genres</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Tags">Tags</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Features">Features</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Developers">Developers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Publishers">Publishers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Age">Age</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Region">Region</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Categories">Categories</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SpecialFields">Special fields</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SortingName">Sorting name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Links">Links</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_CompaniesLimitHelp">For companies, the recommended value is 1: the plugin tries to store only the main developer/publisher and avoid support, porting, multiplayer or regional distribution studios.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SortingLinksHelp">Sorting name is calculated locally: it detects sequels with 2/3, II/III or v2/v3 and generates values like Base name 01, 02, 03. Links try to use official URLs; if the game comes from Steam and has an AppId, the store URL is added reliably.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TagPrefix">Tag prefix</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TagPrefixHelp">If you enter a prefix, it is added before each new tag. Example: AI: Open world.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_CategoryPrefix">Category prefix</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_CategoryPrefixHelp">Useful to group categories created by the plugin. Example: Meta: Action.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_Blacklist">Term blacklist</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_BlacklistHelp">Enter words or phrases separated by commas, semicolons, or line breaks. Any generated tag, genre, feature, category, developer, publisher, age rating, or region containing one of these terms is discarded before it can be applied. Use it to block vague, unwanted, duplicated, or incorrectly translated vocabulary.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_EnableTemplateRules">Enable automatic template rules</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_EnableTemplateRulesHelp">If disabled, the plugin always uses the selected template from the Templates tab. If enabled, source, platform or type rules can replace it automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_GenreTemplateRules">Template rules by game type</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_GenreTemplateRulesHelp">Used to automatically choose a template based on game type. The plugin searches for the term in current genres, tags and categories. Format: term=TemplateName. If it finds a match, it uses that template instead of the active one. Example: RPG=RPG.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_PlatformRules">Rules by platform</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_PlatformRulesHelp">Used to choose a template based on the game's platform. It has priority over game type rules. Format: Platform=TemplateName. Example: Nintendo Switch=Short. Useful for shorter handheld descriptions, more technical PC text or special emulation templates.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceRules">Rules by source</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_SourceRulesHelp">Used to choose a template based on the source or library the game was imported from, for example Steam, GOG, Epic, Xbox, PlayStation or a custom source. It has priority over platform and type. Format: Source=TemplateName. Example: Steam=Long.</sys:String>
